      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Divya / Charan thanks for the patch. I found a similar but slightly different issue in the accounting. Could you open a bug for discussion. \n\n\nFor this patch:\n\nCould you help me understand where we end up including the shmem pages in cached?\n\nMy understanding is that shmem pages are swap backed\n\nhttps://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/196145c606d0f816fd3926483cb1ff87e09c2c0b/fs/proc/task_mmu.c#L696-L697\n\n```c\n    else if (folio_test_swapbacked(folio))\n        mss-\u003epss_shmem +\u003d pss;\n```\n\ni.e. a page cannot be in the swap cache unless it is swap backed\n\nIf we had to allocate page in `shmem_read_folio_gfp()`\nhttps://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/196145c606d0f816fd3926483cb1ff87e09c2c0b/mm/shmem.c#L5178-L5195\n\nthen we mark it swapbacked:\nhttps://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/196145c606d0f816fd3926483cb1ff87e09c2c0b/mm/shmem.c#L1787-L1789\n\n```c\nallocated:\n\t__folio_set_locked(folio);\n\t__folio_set_swapbacked(folio);\n```\n\nFor the cached pages we already removed the swap cache pages.\n\n\nWe can move these into swap cache by `shmem_read_folio` or `do_swpa_page()`.\n\nThe cached accounting already removed the swap cache pages: \n\nhttps://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/196145c606d0f816fd3926483cb1ff87e09c2c0b/fs/proc/meminfo.c#L48-L49\n\n```c\n\tcached \u003d global_node_page_state(NR_FILE_PAGES) -\n\t\t\ttotal_swapcache_pages() - i.bufferram;\n```\n\nSo I think there is a double accounting but not for all shmem pages just the portion -- `Total Swap Backed - Total Swap Cache`\n\n\nI\u0027d like to discuss further in bug since we have similar but slightly differnt issue we were investigating.\n\nThanks,  \nKalesh",
